  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Isolated to scattered diurnal showers are \nexpected will occur across the Northeastern 1/4 of the CWA \ntoday/tonight as a deepening surface/upper level low moves \nslowly over the Southern New England Coast. Otherwise, drying \ntrend to wrap up the week.\n\nNorthwest flow/wraparound moisture rotating around the western\nside of a deepening trough and slow moving sfc/upper low will\ncontinue to promote the development of stratocu across much of\nthe region. A vort max pivoting through the western edge of the\nupper low will cross the region this afternoon and evening \nwhich should help to trigger a few showers over northeast PA. \nHigh temps today will vary from the upper 60s across the \nNorthern Mtns to the low 80s in the Southeast.\n\nThe upper low begins to move off to the east tomorrow, though a\nfew showers may linger through the first half of the day. \nExpect drier conditions for Friday and Saturday. Chances for \nshowers and thunderstorms increase Saturday night through Sunday\nahead of an approaching shortwave, but there are still \nconsiderable differences regarding the timing of this feature.",
